## 2026-08-25 — login/reset serialization correction

- Security review found that the login handler discarded the session created under `authenticateAndCreateSession()`'s Tracker credential lock and created a second session after releasing that lock. A password reset in that interval could revoke the first session before the second old-password session was written.
- Commit `789f4b061908fb0b3987b61110d812e6be47941e` returns the locked session directly and adds a regression test requiring exactly one session creation for successful login. `npm run check` passed 115 portable tests, deterministic build passed 27 artifacts, production/full audits reported zero vulnerabilities, and Dockerfile/Compose checks passed.
- Built `watch-tracker:verify` at `sha256:d80423d49feec5f471ea87ee9da195bc7a9ad0eef14f0a553dfdf4163debcc02` and recreated only `watch-tracker-lan-foundation-app-1` with `--no-deps`; the existing database container and volumes were not touched. App health and live `/ready` are green. `/reset-password` has no-store/no-referrer and restrictive CSP; an invalid live reset request returned only generic `400 password-reset.invalid`.
- Core PR #4 exact head `5bfd7a219a846d21dc58acd87741c027e5d1ef43` passed Validate Core run `32795828024`, including the isolated PostgreSQL/migration gate, image scans, SBOM, and disposable Compose smoke. Chromium-family browser automation is still unavailable, so no authenticated latest-head browser proof was fabricated. Historical audit remains **FAIL**; no release, tag, or merge occurred.

